 of papillary growth and atypia  to foci of clear cut DCIS  A small focus of invasive carcinoma  measuring 0 4cm is also present in association with the DCIS on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  in a micro invasive or minimally invasive pattern  Immunohistochemical stains for p63  myosin  keratin and calponin on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  do not show evidence of invasion in this section  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR   EXCISION  1  FOCAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN MAXIMUM DIAMETER  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED MARGIN   See note   2  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS   See note  3  EXTENSIVE FLORID DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITH AREAS OF PAPILLARY HYPERPLASIA AND ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA Note  The focus of DCIS is present in a background of extensive hyperplasia similar to that seen in main specimen  An Immunohistochemical stain for cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  demonstrates staining throughout the papillary lesion supporting a diagnosis of papilloma  Additionally  immunohistochemical stains for p63  myosin  keratin and calponin on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  does not show evidence of invasion and confirm the diagnosis of an intraductal papilloma  The slides were reviewed at the Breast Pathology conference on REMOVED_DATE  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN DEEP   EXCISION  1  FLORID DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  USUAL TYPE 2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA 3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR   EXCISION  1  FLORID DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  USUAL TYPE 2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA 3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN LATERAL   EXCISION  1  FLORID DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  USUAL TYPE 2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH SCLEROSING 