 In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 MAY 97 at 14 42     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two specimens  Labeled  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibroadipose tissue fragment  inked and sectioned to reveal predominantly fibrous cut surface without distinct mass lesions  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  The remainder is entirely submitted in cassettes A through D  Labeled  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm soft tissue fragment  inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous and fatty cut surfaces  without distinct mass lesion  A representative section is frozen as FX  2  and submitted in J  The reminder of the specimen is entirely submitted in E through I  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINO