cal assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of breast with an incision into the specimen  The specimen is inked such that only the true margins bear ink  Inspection reveals an approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm tan  firm  lobulated  well circumscribed mass with central and eccentric white stellate lesion which grossly approaches several margins  The tissue surrounding the mass is white and irregularly dense  Entire mass and representative surrounding tissue are submitted in cassettes A J  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST MASS  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
