Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 54 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST MASS  LEFT   WIDE EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  AS MEASURED FROM A GLASS SLIDE  WITH CENTRAL HYALINIZING FIBROSIS AND NECROSIS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE WITHIN AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS  LYMPH NODES   LEFT AXILLA  DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 15 OUT OF 15 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY LEFT   TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 6 OUT OF 6 LYMPH NODES  BREAST  ADDITIONAL DEEP   RE EXCISION  BREAST TISSUE WITH STROMAL FIBROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR TO DEEP MARGIN   CAUTERIZED BREAST TISSUE WITH INVOLUTIONAL CHANGE AND FOCAL MICROCALIFICATIONS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  No definite lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is seen  although several suspicious foci are identified  The examined margin of resection appears free of carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 01                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See Note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in multiple parts  Labeled  wide excision  left breast  and received fresh from the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  There is a short stitch and a long stitch designating the superior and the lateral margins resectively  The superior margin is inked in green and lateral in red  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm  ill defined nodule  present at 0 2cm from the closest inferior margin  A representative section of the nodule and inferior margin is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in cassette A  B to D are tumor with additional inferior margins  E to H are sections of superior margin  I and J are sections of the lateral and medial margins submitted en face  Labeled  left axillary contents  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fatty tissue are multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in maximum dimension and disected from this fatty tissue which is submitted in cassettes K V  Cassettes M V contain half of each lymph node  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  and consist