 compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 37     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The poorly differentiated tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 06 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  R breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm unoriented piece of fibroadipose tissue and a second smaller REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm  tan lesion in the parenchyma that abuts the resection margin on several aspects  A second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm ill defined  firm tan lesion is present  also abutting the resection margin  the two masses appear contiguous  The first lesion is entirely submitted in A  The second lesion is entirely submitted in B C  The small fragment of fibroadipose tissue is bisected and submitted entirely in D  Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCE