Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 12 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast calcifications                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  COMEDO TYPE  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT ON FIVE OF TEN SECTIONS  SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  AND EXTENDING FOCALLY TO AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  ANTERIOR   NOTE  No stromal  lymphatic or vascular invasion is present  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  PRESENT IN FIVE OF FIVE SECTIONS  REPRESENTING THREE FRAGMENTS   EXTENDING TO THE EDGES OF THE BIOPSY  NOTE  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  No in situ tumor is identified  Because the biopsy is received as three fragments  the actual size and status of margins cannot be assessed  The tumor diameters on the two largest fragments are 0 9cm and 1 3cm  respectively  measured from slides  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 52 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fibrofatty tissue with a short stitch marking the superior margin and a long stitch marking the lateral margin  The anterior surface is inked black and the deep  posterior  surface is inked blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal fibrofatty parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely from lateral to medial in A through J  Another specimen is received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  and consists of three fibrofatty tissues measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm in aggregate  One of these fragments has a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm very firm  white  fibrous  ill defined nodule  This nodule is fully submitted in K and L  The second fragment also has a firm  white fibrous area measuring 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  and is somewhat stellate shaped  Fully submitted in M and N  The last fragment appears to be purely adipose tissue and is fully submitted in O  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  NO AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                