100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a simple mastectomy specimen containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm irregularly shaped  white  firm mass with white fibrous strands radiating away from the center  The mass appears to be located mainly in the anterior and inferior portion of the resected specimen  A second firm mass is located approximately 1 5cm lateral and 1cm superior to the previously described mass  The second mass has a 0 5cm brown colored core surrounded by 0 1cm light tan colored shell  The second mass is located at 1 2cm away from the posterior deep resection margin  SECTION CODE A  Section of first tumor mass at its closest margin  anterior inferior margin   B  Body of the first tumor mass  C  Section containing the second tumor mass on the lateral side near the deep  posterior  resection margin  D  Another section containing the center of the second mass  E  Section on the lateral end of the specimen containing some fibrous tissue at the posterior resection margin  Seven lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail  ranging in size from 0 5cm up to 2 2cm in length  The four larger nodes are bisected in half and the three smaller nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes F to H  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Randall David Gaz  M D  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
