Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 52 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm stellate  firm  gritty area abutting multiple margins  The gritty area is submitted in A  remainder of breast in B D  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SUSPICIOUS AREA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
