irm gritty tissue in H  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is appropriate for age  with fibrocystic changes  cysts up to 0 8cm in diameter   representative sections in I through K  Multiple unremarkable lymph nodes of up to 1 0cm are identified in the axillary fat  submitted in L through P  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 44 CLINICAL DATA  Question invasive carcinoma  Margins please                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  50   SEE NOTE   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  50    FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CYST FORMATION AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS   MICROCALCIFICATIONS  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL LATERAL AND POSTERIOR MARGINS   EXCISION  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 1cm in greatest diameter  It involves the deep margin  The specimen designated   additional lateral and posterior margins   is involved with infiltrating ductal carcinoma  10   and intraductal carcinoma  90   on one edge  but it does not extend through the specimen  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  FIFTEEN LYMPH NODES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  LEVEL II   EXCISION  TWO LYMPH NODES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 16                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 7cm piece of breast tissue with an attached ellipse of skin which measures REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  There is a short silk suture at the superior margin and a long silk suture at the lateral margin  The specimen is inked  anterior designated yellow  and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm poorly defined  white  firm  gritty area which involves the deep margin and comes to within 0 8cm of the inferior margin  A representative section of the deep resection margin is frozen as FS 1 and saved frozen  A representative section of the inferior resection margin is frozen as FS 3  now A  Representative serial sections from lateral to medial are submitted in B through H  with B through E being the lateral half and the remainder being the medial half  Labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  right breast additional lateral and posterior margins   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous tissue with multiple cysts up to 0 3cm  Submitted entirely in I through S  Labeled  right axilla nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fatty tissue  from which multiple tan  rubbery lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm are dissected  portions of these lymph nodes are submitted in T through V  Labeled  Level II   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fatty tissue  from which two lymph nodes  each 0 3cm  is dissected  The nodes are submitted in W  and the remainder in X  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 2  BREAST RIGHT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  SOME IS COMEDO  TYPE   CARCINOMA APPROACHES TO WITHIN 0 1CM OF DEEP MARGIN  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST TISSUE PART B  ADDITIONAL LATERAL   POSTERIOR MARGINS  RIGHT BREA PART C  AXILLA NODES  RIGHT  PART D  LEVEL II , Unchecked.
