r size can be influenced by treatment changes and may appear less than the pre treatment tumor measurements  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 14 LYMPH NODES  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm irregular portion of fibroadipose tissue with an inserted wire  A short stitch denotes the superior margin and a long stitch the lateral margin  The anterior margin is marked with blue ink  the posterior margin with black ink  the superior margin with green ink and the inferior margin with yellow ink  The specimen is serially sectioned from the lateral to the medial aspect to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fairly well circumscribed  firm  tan nodule which is located adjacent to the clip  The nodule extends to 0 2cm of the anterior margin  and 0 7cm to the posterior margin  1 5cm to the superior margin  1 2cm to the inferior margin  1 0cm to the lateral margin and 3 0cm to the medial margin  The remainder of the tissue consists mainly of soft  white fibrous tissue and the specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the nodule in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The lesion is in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the area of microcalcification is in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm irregular lobular portion of fatty tissue  within which multiple tan pink lymph nodes are identified  The lymph nodes are submitted in their entirety as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four lymph nodes   REMOV