Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 43 CLINICAL DATA  History of mother with breast cancer  Mammogram with new abnormality in central portion of the right breast  FNA was non diagnostic  Now presents for excisional breast biopsy  On physical exam no palpable masses in either breast and no adenopathy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  70    MODERATELY TO FOCALLY POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  ABOUT 1 CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  FOCALLY PRESENT AT THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  30    CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  SEE NOTE   2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Estrogen and progesterone receptor studies will be reported on in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 37                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 32     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm semifirm  tan yellow breast biopsy with localizing wire in place and accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm white  poorly circumscribed lesion  1 0cm in greatest dimension  grossly abutting an inked resection margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is notable for a mixture of white fibrous tissue and soft yellow adipose tissue  Representative section of lesion is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the lesion is in A through E  remainder of specimen in F through J  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST RIGHT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
