he specimen is inked  as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  Sectioning reveals a lower outer  quadrant biopsy clip within a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm area of irregular fibrosis with no  discrete tumor identified  This region is 1 4cm from the posterior margin and  2 1cm from anterior margin skin  Medial to the clip about 1 2cm away is an  ill defined region of ductular dilatation spanning REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  3 0cm  from the posterior margin and 2 5cm from the anterior margin  0 3cm medial to  that region and 1 5cm away from the clip is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm well  circumscribed  firm  white nodule  The nodule is 3 0cm from the posterior  margin and 2 5cm from the anterior margin  Specimen reviewed with Dr  Lerwill   Sections are submitted as follows      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Clip site and surrounding region of irregular fibrosis    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior and posterior margins closest to clip site    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Ill defined region of ductular dilatation    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 4cm nodule  submitted entirely    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior and posterior margins closet to the nodule     B  Labeled  right mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm mastectomy specimen  oriented by the surgeon with a long stitch designating the lateral position and  a short stitch designating the superior position  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  0 3cm skin ellipse with a nipple appears unremarkable  The specimen is inked  as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  0 3cm well defined  circumscribed  firm  white nodule in the lower inner  quadrant containing a clip  0 9cm from the posterior margin and 3 4cm from the  anterior margin  Centrally within the breast  11 0cm away from nodule  1  is  another firm  white  well circumscribed nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm REMOVED_DATE  cm from the posterior margin and 3 0cm from the anterior margin  4 0cm away  from nodule  2 is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm well defined  well circumscribed firm  nodule  A fourth nodule 1 5cm away from nodule  3 is also well circumscribed  and well defined  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The remainder of the breast  consists of yellow fatty and white fibrous tissue  Specimen reviewed with Dr   Lerwill  Representative sections are submitted as follows  to include all  nodular foci     SECTION CODE    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The lower inner quadrant nodule  entirely submitted  with margins    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Central breast  to include nodules    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper inner quadrant         PART A  BREAST MASTECTOMY  LEFT  PART B  BREAST MASTECTOMY  RIGHT       report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 11 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma  invasive and in situ  with positive margins                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  TWO FOCI  DISTANT FROM THE MARGINS  SEE NOTE   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  Note  Dr  F  Koehrner has reviewed selected slides and concurs  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 21 OF 21 LYMPH NODES  BREAST  LEFT   MASTOPEXY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  RADIAL SCAR  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 46                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  One specimen is received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  and consists of a 24 x 20 x 2 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen  oriented by a long stitch lateral and a short stitch superior  There is a 17 x 12cm overlying skin  with an unremarkable nipple areola complex located in the superior portion of the ellipse  and a 3 0cm  vertical  well healed scar  located 7 5cm inferior and lateral to the nipple  Cross sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm solid  stellate shaped biopsy cavity located beneath the scar  1 5cm from the deep margin  and 0 6cm from the anterior margin  The biopsy site is focally very firm  and tan yellow  with hemorrhage and softer white fibrous tissue extending from the site  Further cross sectioning reveals two focally gritty areas  within 1 2cm of each other  and 0 3cm from the deep margin  located lateral and superior to the biopsy site  Further cross sectioning reveals diffuse fibrocystic changes  Section code  A  Biopsy cavity with deep margin  B  Biopsy cavity with anterior margin  C G  Sections of biopsy site  H  Gritty area lateral to biopsy site  I K  Fibrocystic areas  The axillary tail is dissected for lymph nodes  which are submitted in L T  with L containing sections of a single node  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm aggregate of irregular breast tissues  some with overlying skin  Cross sectioning reveals mixed fibrous and fatty tissue  with scattered microcysts  Representative sections are in U through DD  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Rosen  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT AXILLARY   CONTENTS PART B  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
