Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 45 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  THREE NODULES  REMOVED_DATE TO REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 3 OF 21 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of tumor  The metastatic foci spans less than 0 2cm and do not transgress the lymph node capsule  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for etrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone recptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 45     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a modified radical mastectomy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm with axillary tail measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The skin ellipse  with nipple  measures REMOVED_DATE x 14 5cm  There is an ill defined hard nodule  tumor  1  inferior to the nipple measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal two other masses  One is located inferior and medial to the nipple  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm located 0 5cm from the inferior margin  tumor  2   The third   tumor  3  irregularly shaped white firm nodule is located deep to the second nodule  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm  and is located 0 3cm from the closest inferior margin  Section Code  A B  first tumor inferior to the nipple  tumor to skin  C D  first tumor to normal breast  E  second tumor to closest margin  F H  second tumor to normal breast  I  third nodule  closest margin  J  third tumor to normal breast  In the axillary tail there are 19 tan rubbery nodules ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are entirely submitted in cassettes K through N  Representative section of normal breast in cassette O  Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
