r approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  20 AUG 03 at 14 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast stitch at 12 o clock   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 15 3cm mastectomy with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE attached skin with nipple  The areola is 4 3cm in diameter and the nipple is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The skin of the specimen is mottled overlying a mass which largely replaces the breast parenchyma  The mass measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm  The mass is tan and fleshy with a large central cystic area containing necrotic debris and bloody fluid  There are several polypoid projections into the cyst  The mass abuts the posterior margin and overlying skin anteriorly  The tumor grossly abuts the anterior surgical margin as well  The posterior surgical margin is inked black and the anterior surgical margin is inked blue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Tumor to skin  C F  Tumor to deep margin  G  Tumor to posterior and anterior margins  H J  Polypoid excrescences  K P  Solid tumor  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrofatty tissue  Out of this tissue are 15 firm nodular fragments of tan soft tissue ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Seven nodules were sectioned and individually submitted entirely in cassettes Q W  Eight smaller nodules were submitted four to a cassette in cassettes X and Y  Resident  CHRISTOPHER M  WILLIAM  MD   Ph D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Alphonse Taghian  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  MODI