ctioned from the anterior to the posterior aspect to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm  tan lesion with ill defined borders which extends to 0 2cm of the inferior margin  0 8cm to the superior margin  0 6cm to the lateral margin  1 8cm to the medial margin  1 3cm to the anterior margin and 2 3cm to the posterior margin  The remainder of the tissue consists mainly of adipose tissue with a scant amount of soft  white fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  from the anterior to the posterior aspect  with the lesion in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Tim Robinson  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Unchecked.
